---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Sam's moods
description: The moods Sam comes in, and the name to use for each one on a post.
permalink: /sam/
noindex: true
---
{%- set rows = [
  ["breakdown", "What they just said: an update"],
  ["translation", "What they just said: a translation"],
  ["howto", "How not to stuff this up"],
  ["hottake", "Hot take"],
  ["tip", "Did you know?"],
  ["realtalk", "Looking after you"]
] -%}
<main class="archive">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="archive-head">
      <a class="back" href="/">← Home</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Sam's moods</p>
      <h1>Pick a Sam for every post.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Add a <code>sam:</code> line to a post with one of the names below. Leave it out and the post gets the usual Sam for its type. Write <code>sam: none</code> to leave him off.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="moods">
      {% for key, m in samMoods.moods %}
      <figure class="mood">
        <svg class="mood-sam anim-{{ m.anim }}" viewBox="0 0 300 244" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#{{ m.symbol }}"/></svg>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>{{ m.name }}</h2>
          <code>sam: {{ key }}</code>
          <p>{{ m.use }}</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <section class="defaults">
      <h2>The usual Sam for each post type</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Post type</th><th scope="col">Sam</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for r in rows %}{% set d = samMoods.moods[samMoods.defaults[r[0]]] %}<tr><td>{{ r[1] }}</td><td>{{ d.name if d else "No Sam, an arrow instead" }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">These are working sketches. The designer's final artwork will keep the same names, so posts won't need changing.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
